<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">24 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 24 June, from 474 to 1948.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">474 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,552 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Western Roman emperor Glycerius is forced to abdicate</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Glycerius, proclaimed emperor of the West in March 473 by the magister militum <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gundobad">Gundobad</a> and not recognised by the Eastern emperor Leo I, was forced to abdicate. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-roman-empire">Western Roman Empire</a> ended in 476, when the last emperor was deposed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-roman-empire">Western Roman Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-i-of-portugal" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/afonso-i-of-portugal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1128">1128 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">898 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Afonso Henriques defeats his mother's forces at São Mamede</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guimaraes">Guimarães</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-i-of-portugal">Afonso Henriques</a> defeated the forces of his mother, Countess Teresa, and her Galician ally Fernão Peres de Trava. The victory gave him control of the County of Portugal and is traditionally seen as the founding event of Portuguese independence.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sao-mamede">Battle of São Mamede</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-i-of-portugal">Afonso I of Portugal</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teresa-countess-of-portugal">Teresa, Countess of Portugal</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1314">1314 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">712 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert the Bruce routs Edward II at Bannockburn</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the second day, Scottish spearmen drove the English army into the burns and marshes near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stirling">Stirling</a>. Edward II fled, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>'s independence was secured until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> recognised it in 1328.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1340">1340 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">686 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward III destroys the French fleet at Sluys</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The English fleet of King Edward III attacked the French fleet assembled for an invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwin">Zwin</a> estuary off Sluis, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>, and destroyed it almost entirely. The victory gave England control of the Channel for years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sluys">Battle of Sluys</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-iii-of-england">Edward III of England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1374 CE <span class="tih-ago">652 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">An outbreak of dancing mania begins in Aachen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">One of the biggest outbreaks of dancing mania, in which groups of people danced erratically, allegedly until they collapsed from exhaustion, began in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aachen">Aachen</a>. It spread to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metz">Metz</a>, Strasbourg, Utrecht and other places, and to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aachen">Aachen</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1497">1497 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">529 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Cabot makes landfall in North America</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Sailing for Henry VII, the Venetian navigator <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-cabot">John Cabot</a> landed on the coast, probably of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a> or Cape Breton. His voyage became the basis of later English claims in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1717">1717 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">309 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Premier Grand Lodge of England is founded</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Four <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> lodges met at the Goose and Gridiron alehouse to form a Grand Lodge. It marks the beginning of organised modern Freemasonry.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1812">1812 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">214 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon's Grande Armée crosses the Niemen into Russia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 450,000 troops in the first wave crossed into Russian territory. By December only a fraction had survived the retreat from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grande-armee">Grande Armée</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1948">1948 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">78 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet Union begins the Berlin Blockade</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet forces cut road, rail and canal links to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-berlin">West Berlin</a>. The Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> responded with an airlift that supplied the city's two million people for eleven months.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></div></li></ol>
